    "bio": "Prof. Sarah Chen is a leading psychiatrist and neuroscientist at UNSW Sydney and the Randwick Health & Innovation Precinct. Her work focuses on treatment-resistant depression and neurostimulation therapies, including transcranial magnetic stimulation (TMS) and ketamine-based approaches.\n\nShe leads the Precinct's Treatment-Resistant Depression Clinic at Prince of Wales Hospital and has established one of Australia's largest clinical trial programmes in neurostimulation. Her research bridges mechanistic neuroscience with real-world clinical outcomes.\n\nProf. Chen has published over 140 peer-reviewed articles and holds several patents related to neurostimulation device protocols and patient monitoring systems.",
